\pard\b\f0\fs24 Protectant Flag Ship Balaenoptera\b0\f1\fs18\par
\b\f0\par
Capacity:\b0\f1  Large flagship / colonial conversion; exact complement not stated.\par
\b\f0 Role in Story:\b0\f1  Protectant command ship, training platform and political stage for Marcellus and Ava.\par
\b\f0 Related Characters:\b0\f1  John Walker, Marcellus Athos, Lady Ava, Tor Engineer, the recruit class.\par
\b\f0 Season:\b0\f1  Chapters 1-2.\par
\b\f0 Unique Features:\b0\f1  Concave projectile-deflecting hull, vast halls, modular turrets that can swap between PDC, EMP, defence rail and recovery roles.\par
\b\f0 Description:\b0\f1  The Balaenoptera began as a regional orbital defence ship and was later re-engineered for colonial and policing work. Its architecture feels like the rib cage of a giant winged whale. Even when docked, it projects authority, scale and institutional power.\par
\b\f0 Sights:\b0\f1  Curving structural pillars, bright hull ranges, bridge windows over Ceres and open transit halls.\par
\b\f0 Sounds:\b0\f1  Airlock hisses, training-range fire systems, bridge chatter and the steady hum of a capital ship at dock.\par
\b\f0 Smell:\b0\f1  Warm human-friendly air after cold airlocks, printed food from the mess, and clean recycled shipboard air.\par
\b\f0 Notes:\b0\f1  John uses the ship for recruit training and EVA drills before the lost-facility deployment.\par
\b\f0 Built at:\b0\f1  Protectant orbital defence program.\par
